# sys-apps/policycoreutils cross-compile fixups — see env/policycoreutils-cross.conf
# Its setfiles/ component uses a hand-written Makefile (no econf), so it never
# receives portage's auto --with-sysroot and calls bare host pkg-config. The env
# file bakes --sysroot=${ESYSROOT} into CC (fixes <stdio.h>/<fts.h> not found) and
# routes pkg-config through the crossdev wrapper at the target sysroot (fixes
# "Package 'libselinux'/'libsemanage' not found"). Scoped here so the --sysroot CC
# override and PKG_CONFIG_* don't leak into the 100+ econf packages that already
# get the sysroot correctly from econf's --with-sysroot.
sys-apps/policycoreutils policycoreutils-cross.conf
